@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    At <strong>ForSoma Book Store</strong>, we value the privacy, security, and trust of our users.
    Our platform is designed to help students buy, sell, exchange, and request academic textbooks
    in a safe and convenient environment. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use,
    protect, and manage the information you provide while using our services.
</p>

<h2>Information We Collect</h2>

<p>
    To provide and improve our services, we may collect certain information when you create an account,
    post textbook listings, submit wanted advertisements, make offers, complete transactions, or leave reviews.
    This information may include:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Your name and email address.</li>
    <li>Institution, campus, and student-related information.</li>
    <li>Textbook listings and wanted advertisements.</li>
    <li>Offers, transaction records, and review history.</li>
    <li>Information necessary to facilitate communication between users.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>

<p>
    The information collected is used solely for legitimate platform purposes, including:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Creating and managing user accounts.</li>
    <li>Facilitating textbook transactions between students.</li>
    <li>Providing customer support and responding to inquiries.</li>
    <li>Improving platform functionality and user experience.</li>
    <li>Maintaining a secure and trustworthy marketplace environment.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Information Sharing</h2>

<p>
    ForSoma does not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for
    advertising or marketing purposes. Information is only shared when necessary to enable
    interactions between users or when required by law.
</p>

<p>
    User-generated content, including textbook listings, wanted advertisements, reviews,
    and profile information, may be visible to other registered users of the platform.
    Users are responsible for ensuring that they do not publish sensitive personal information
    that they do not wish to make publicly available.
</p>

<h2>Data Security</h2>

<p>
    We implement reasonable technical and administrative measures to protect user information
    from unauthorized access, misuse, disclosure, alteration, or destruction. While we strive
    to maintain a secure environment, no online platform can guarantee absolute security.
    Users are encouraged to use strong passwords and exercise caution when communicating with others.
</p>

<h2>Campus Trading Safety</h2>

<p>
    ForSoma promotes safe trading practices among students. We encourage users to meet in public,
    well-monitored campus locations when exchanging textbooks or completing transactions.
    Recommended meeting locations include:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Campus Libraries</li>
    <li>Student Centres</li>
    <li>Campus Reception Areas</li>
    <li>Other designated public study spaces</li>
</ul>

<h2>Your Rights and Responsibilities</h2>

<p>
    Users have the right to access, update, and manage their account information. By using
    ForSoma Book Store, you agree to provide accurate information and to use the platform
    responsibly and in accordance with applicable laws and university policies.
</p>

<h2>Policy Updates</h2>

<p>
    This Privacy Policy may be updated periodically as the platform evolves. Any changes will
    be published on this page. Continued use of the platform following the publication of
    updates constitutes acceptance of the revised Privacy Policy.
</p>

<h2>Contact Us</h2>

<p>
    If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy,
    please contact the ForSoma support team through the platform's support channels.
</p>

<hr />

<h2>Disclaimer</h2>

<p>
    <strong>ForSoma Book Store</strong> serves solely as a platform that connects buyers and sellers.
    ForSoma is not directly involved in transactions between users and cannot guarantee the quality,
    condition, accuracy, availability, pricing, delivery, or suitability of any textbook or item
    listed on the platform.
</p>

<p>
    All transactions are conducted at the discretion and risk of the participating users.
    Users are responsible for verifying information, inspecting items, and ensuring that
    arrangements made with other users meet their expectations and requirements.
</p>

<p>
    ForSoma shall not be liable for any loss, damage, dispute, fraud, injury, or inconvenience
    arising from interactions or transactions conducted through the platform.
</p>